  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nKeen readers may note the lack of notably different discussions\nrecently and this latest discussion offers little to change that\ntrend. The combination of surface high pressure and ridging\naloft over a multi-day period (with very high confidence) means\nthe weather story is a bit monotonous. So continue to enjoy \nabove normal temperature (with large diurnal swings), light \nwinds, abundant sunshine and dry weather.\n\nMore variance in the upper level pattern from ensemble models \nstarting around Thursday through the following Monday (November \n2nd) suggests some topics of discussion but with little \nconfidence at this point. This includes weak shortwave movement\nnorth of the region Thursday into Friday morning (offering 30% \nor less probabilities for measurable rain mainly in NW PA);\nunlikely waves Friday into Saturday (offering less than 20%\nmeasurable rain probabilities); and the potential strong trough\npassage Sunday into Monday (higher likelihood of rain but timing\nof its arrival has slowly be inching later). Clarity will arrive\neventually but for now, nothing merits further discussion.",
